  "limits": [
    "Exact bounded static native bytes, not native execution, actual Yi dispatch, live shader selection or visual parity.",
    "Type and field names are FNV/layout candidates; hashes neither exclude collisions nor authenticate native literal names.",
    "Ray registration, both constructors, the virtual slot and a definition-primitive dispatch site identify this builder. The native producers of its context, transforms, clocks, color, UV modes, frames and 44-byte draw records remain unresolved.",
    "Float32 arithmetic and half conversion retain the native floating-point environment. Nearest-even half examples would be conditional on FPCR; no live FPCR is measured.",
    "Ray colors and the separate fast quad packer have different rounding/clamping paths. No application color or ray behavior is changed by this witness.",
    "Missing historical LLVM archives remain missing; the inline bytes and static exploration are additional evidence only.",
    "The accepted application remains at 3086 passing tests out of 3088, the same two baseline failures, seven browser cases, fifteen exact packet pixel cases and the accepted production pack.",
    "The generic native builder consumes prepared draw/transform records; this witness does not attest their mapping to authored size, color, frame and lookup controls."
  ],
  "diagnostics": [
    "A first exploratory script was named inspect.py and shadowed the Python standard-library module needed by Capstone. It was renamed before the inspection completed.",
    "The first type-search prototype omitted the struct import; it was corrected before results were produced.",
    "Two selected instruction checks and finite-color wording were added after the first untracked record draft. The immutable-output writer rejected the changed draft; that draft was archived in the cache and the final record regenerated. The initial exact-record guard consequently failed; the final 106-case normal and optimized runs both pass.",
    "A naive mapping from draw-record scale fields to authored birthScale0 would make the retained source ray degenerate. This is treated as evidence that producer-side mapping remains unresolved, not as authorization to reorder game data or geometry."
  ],
